cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Cross-Engine Citation Study, rounds one and two: sources and brands cited by
  ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Google's AI Overview
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Minel
    family-names: Gunesoglu
    affiliation: Is My Brand in AI
    email: minel@ismybrandinai.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4823-6016'
abstract: >-
  Twelve B2B SaaS buyer questions were put by hand to ChatGPT, Perplexity,
  Gemini and Google's AI Overview, one run per engine-question pair, and every
  source each engine displayed was recorded in order. Round one, 19 June 2026,
  recorded sources only over 27 runs. Round two, collected on 6 to 7 August
  2026 and published on 9 August 2026, recorded
  sources with a type code and the brands each answer recommended, in order,
  over 48 runs covering every question on every engine. On the seven open
  recommendation and alternatives questions of round two, the four engines
  agreed on 32 per cent of the brands they recommended and 1 per cent of the
  sources they cited (Jaccard similarity). Round two logged 322 citations of 193
  distinct sources, 78.2 per cent of them cited by one engine only. Of the 80
  distinct sources Perplexity cited in June, 42 were still cited in August. The
  per-run rows of both rounds and a script that recounts every published figure
  are included.
keywords:
  - AI search
  - citation
  - generative engine optimization
  - ChatGPT
  - Perplexity
  - Gemini
  - Google AI Overviews
  - brand recommendation
  - B2B SaaS
